{
  "summary": "Adds a `rebroadcastwallettx` RPC method and a corresponding GUI context menu action to allow users to manually rebroadcast an unconfirmed wallet transaction. Users can trigger rebroadcast directly by txid instead of manually retrieving the transaction hex and passing it to `sendrawtransaction`.",
  "problem": "Users have no direct mechanism in the wallet RPC or GUI to re-announce an unconfirmed transaction that failed to propagate or dropped out of mempools. The current workaround requires manually extracting the raw transaction hex and calling `sendrawtransaction`.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'From the discussion in #36403, it is clear that there needs to be a way for users to rebroadcast a transaction. Currently, the way to do so requires getting the raw transaction, getting the hex, and using sendrawtransaction.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Adds a new wallet RPC endpoint and adds a context menu option in the Qt GUI transaction table.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Adds a rebroadcastwallettx RPC command and a GUI menu action allowing users to manually rebroadcast a specific unconfirmed wallet transaction by txid. Previously, manual rebroadcast required fetching the raw transaction hex and submitting it via sendrawtransaction. The addition was motivated by broader discussions around transaction rebroadcasting architecture in #36403.",
